sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Trushko et al. (2020) Dev. Cell & Hannezo et al. (2014) PNAS Föppl-von Kármán / 3D triangulated-shell spherical epithelial cyst buckling under alginate confinement — MorphoEval overall 75.4/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) remediated evaluation of `2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py`. The single v2 remediation item is closed: a free 3D triangulated shell with apical-basal spontaneous curvature, Winkler capsule wall and self-contact (`solve_confined_cyst_shell3d`) now runs beside the 2D ring, reproduces the Fig. 2E pressure trajectory from capsule dilation (r = 0.939, RMSE 0.089 kPa), keeps the unconfined control spherical (delta/R0 = 0.005, 0 folds), responds to the dGamma sweep in the Hannezo direction and is backed by 2 new Lean theorems (7 total, 0 sorry). It also exposes that the 2D ring which carried the v2 scores is a prescribed Gaussian profile rescaled to a fitted target depth, that the free solver under-predicts the WT fold depth (0.30 vs 0.64 R0) with 12 mesh-templated shallow folds instead of 1, that dGamma is calibrated rather than measured, and that the specimen is a thyroid follicle whose circularity (0.848) the v2 audit misreported as 0.654. The overall score therefore goes DOWN from 93.3 while the model is more honest and more capable. Overall 75.4/100 (faithfulness 70.4, reproducibility 87.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8a7928d7; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 76, Morphological realism / specimen match 62, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 68, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/epithelioid_cyst_buckling_comparison.png: rendered output of 2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py at 8a7928d7, image/png, 721749 B, 2015×1248 px, artifact_sha256 4ca4141a24ffa678e66ef0aa95f8a49938ef52097c632502dde815a62032dd0b (sha256 4ca4141a24ffa678e66ef0aa95f8a49938ef52097c632502dde815a62032dd0b), spec_fingerprint 8c51faae6711c461b674cf68b978bc7ce168e67b48347c008c6f0f5cae0506b9. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 8c51faae6711c461b674cf68b978bc7ce168e67b48347c008c6f0f5cae0506b9; artifact_sha256: 4ca4141a24ffa678e66ef0aa95f8a49938ef52097c632502dde815a62032dd0b; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/epithelioid_cyst_buckling/epithelioid_cyst_buckling_reference.json=c1412a6f1bcc24be..., datasets/epithelioid_cyst_buckling/epithelioid_cyst_specimen.jpg=ec5b534f7a3a8182..., datasets/epithelioid_cyst_buckling/paper_citations.bib=b14ab196e08a46d4..., datasets/epithelioid_cyst_buckling/scout_manifest.json=3d03ec2877bdf349...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-epithelioid-cyst-buckling-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Trushko et al. (2020): an MDCK II monolayer growing to confluence inside a 5 kPa alginate microcapsule (R0 ~ 100 um, h ~ 10 um) buckles into a single deep inward fold once the confinement pressure reaches the Zoelly threshold P_c = 2 E h^2 / (sqrt(3 (1 - nu^2)) R0^2); the fold depth and the capsule pressure read from capsule dilation grow over ~11 h post-confluence (Fig. 2E); Blebbistatin reduces and soft (0.4 kPa) capsules abolish the fold | Hannezo, Prost & Joanny (2014): an apical-basal tension difference dGamma in a monolayer of thickness h induces a spontaneous curvature H0 ~ dGamma / (kappa / h) and selects the sign of folding | Zoelly (1915): the critical external pressure of a thin elastic spherical shell scales as (h / R0)^2; reconstructed_in_script: Zoelly critical pressure and its (h/R0)^2 scaling over a 12-capsule table, an alginate Winkler capsule stiffness, a critical growth stretch g_c and buckling time, a prescribed-profile 2D equatorial ring (mode n in {0, 1, 2}, fitted fold-depth law) with lumen volume partitioning, and (Pass 3) a free 3D icosphere shell with springs, Helfrich bending with apical-basal spontaneous curvature, unilateral capsule contact and self-contact, relaxed quasi-statically in g; WT, Blebbistatin, unconfined and linear-g regimes along the Fig. 2E schedule; a 5-point dGamma sweep; capsule pressure read as K_alg (r_wall / R0 - 1); automated segmentation of a histology micrograph; transfer_boundary: The dataset's g = 2^((t - t_c) / tau_d) is a cell-number (area) ratio; the 3D shell applies sqrt(g) as the linear rest stretch by default while the 2D ring still applies g as a linear perimeter stretch, so the two solvers are not on the same growth convention | dGamma_WT = 4.26 mN/m is calibrated so that H0 R0 = 1 (no apical/basal tension measurement exists in Trushko 2020); the 12-fold 3D pattern coincides with the 12 five-valent icosphere vertices and has not been shown to be mesh-independent | The histology specimen (`epithelioid_cyst_specimen.jpg`) is a thyroid-follicle H&E section, not an MDCK cyst in a capsule; its reference values are attributed loosely to Trushko Fig. 1-2; does_not_claim: A cell-level vertex model with apical/basal/lateral faces, lumen pressure, cell division or T1 transitions; a resolved rigid-cavity (displacement-controlled) buckling threshold for a stiff 68 kPa capsule; a measured apical-basal tension; or a validated single-fold 3D morphology matching the experimental fold depth 0.64 R0." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py:1306-1316 with datasets/epithelioid_cyst_buckling/shell3d_apicobasal_reference.json — dGamma_WT = 4.26 mN/m is calibrated so that H0 R0 = 1 and then reported as a measurement with reference 1.0. Mark it as a calibration (not a measurement) or replace it with a literature apical/basal tension estimate (e.g. MDCK cortical tension measurements) and propagate the uncertainty through the dGamma sweep.",
            "remediation needed: 2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py:1368-1420 and 1440-1458 — p_value / stddev literals (1.0e-12, 1.2e-6, 2.4e-6, 4.8e-6, 1.5e-8, 2.1e-8; 0.045, 0.038, 0.032) are typed, not computed; compute them from the regime table / segmentation or set them to null.",
            "remediation needed: 2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py:201-212 and 248-251 — the 2D ring is a prescribed profile: the fold mode is hard-wired from h/R0 < 0.082, the depth is a fitted law c_delta (g - g_c)^0.68 (1 + 0.22 Gamma) and the L-BFGS-B result is rescaled to that target, so the ring's r = 0.998 trajectory fit is circular. Replace it with a free Föppl-von Kármán ring minimiser (no target_delta, no mode rule) or relabel it as a calibrated empirical profile in the figure titles, measurement `method` strings and the math KG Law 3 entry.",
            "remediation needed: 2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py:421-460 and 487-503 — the WT 12-fold pattern coincides with the 12 five-valent vertices of the subdivision-3 icosphere (mesh-templated). Add a defect-free or random (Fibonacci-sphere + Delaunay) mesh and a subdivision-4 convergence check, and report the fold count only if it is mesh-independent; the fold-detection thresholds 0.35 / 0.04 should be swept too.",
            "remediation needed: 2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py:562-563 and 613-616 — with K_alg = 2.36 kPa from the pinned E_alg = 5 kPa the Winkler wall is as soft as the sheet (k_conf ~ 1.2 Y_2D/R0): fold depth is under-predicted (0.30 vs 0.64 R0) and the capsule dilates 21 % (experiment: a few %), while a stiff 68 kPa capsule does not fold by g = 1.527. Resolve the displacement-controlled (rigid-cavity) vs dead-load threshold, e.g. by a lumen-pressure or volume constraint and a stiff-capsule regime, and reconcile E_alg = 5 kPa with Alessandri 2013.",
            "remediation needed: 2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py:586-589 vs 156-285 — growth-convention inconsistency: the 3D shell reads g = N/N_c as an area ratio (linear stretch sqrt(g)) while the 2D ring reads g as a linear perimeter stretch (area excess g^2). Put both solvers on the same convention (the ring's excess length should be sqrt(g) - 1) and re-derive g_c.",
            "remediation needed: 2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py:984-990 — the panel-D phase diagram DELTA_MAP = min(0.80, 0.728 sqrt(1.52 - g_c) 1.22) is a closed form not produced by any solver; compute the map from the 3D shell (coarse grid, memoised) or label the panel as an analytic sketch.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/epithelioid_cyst_buckling/epithelioid_cyst_specimen.jpg with 2019-trushko-epithelioid-cyst-buckling.py:1436-1460 — the specimen is a thyroid-follicle H&E, not an MDCK cyst in a capsule; the measured circularity is 0.848 (panel F) vs the 0.650 reference attributed to Trushko Fig. 2 (v2 audit reported 0.654). Vendor a CC-licensed MDCK-cyst-in-capsule micrograph (or a Trushko figure under its licence) or relabel the specimen as a generic epithelial-cyst morphology control and drop the Trushko attribution of the 0.650 value." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.754"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (MorphoEval Autonomous Loop Slot 069 Pass 3 Phase B Assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

